  "question": {
    "text": "A plane electromagnetic wave of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo> </mo><mi>MHz</mi></math> travels in free space along the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-direction. At a particular point (in space and time) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of magnetic field at this point is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>",
