    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>At every instant, the ratio of the magnitude of the electric field to the magnitude of the magnetic field in an electromagnetic wave equals the speed of light.</p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p><p>Now, direction of magnetic field can be calculated as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p>"
  }
